{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And I raised up</b> — also 'I placed My spirit upon your sons and they prophesied,' to teach you My statutes. And He mentioned the sons, for if an elder or a sage prophesies, it is not astonishing." "<b>And from your young men</b> — whose nature is to love pleasure and joy — I consecrated them to rebuke you and to sanctify you." "<b>Is this not so?</b> — Can you deny that I did not do this? And because He concluded with the words about the Nazirites, he begins from them, according to the rule of the language."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:49.844202784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}